\pard\sl-240\slmult1 \cf1\lang1033\fs24\f0 Alice's Restaurant Anti-Massacree Adventure\par
\cf2 Thanksgiving 1965.  You are 19 years old.  Since getting booted out of college due to a lack of interest and a corresponding lack of grade points you have been playing music in coffee houses for tips.  You're not sure exactly what you want to do with your life now.  You'd like to make a living playing music, if you could only write a hit song.  But what are the odds of that?  One thing you know for sure, you don't want to go to Vietnam.  Now that you're not a student, they'll be wanting you to go.  With your long hair and a guitar slung over your shoulder, you're hardly the military type.  You're looking forward to spending Thanksgiving with your friend Alice and putting all of this out of your mind.  Alice lives in an old church building and she makes a Thanksgiving dinner that can't be beat.  You have pulled your red VW Microbus up to the side of the building and you are now standing in front of the church.\par
\cf1 \par
open mailbox\par
\cf2 The mailbox is open.  When you open the mailbox an envelope falls out and lands at your feet.\par
\cf1 \par
take envelope\par
\cf2 You have the envelope.\par
\cf1 \par
open envelope\par
\cf2 Opening the envelope reveals a letter.\par
\cf1 \par
read letter\par
\cf2 The letter informs you that you are to report to Whitehall Street in New York for your army physical a week from today.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are at a wooden gothic arched doorway.   You can move east, south and out.\par
\cf1 \par
knock on church door\par
\cf2 Knock.  Knock.    The door opens and reveals Alice.  She immediately hugs you and welcomes you inside.  She apologizes for the mess.  Having all this room where the pews used to be, she hasn't taken out her garbage for a very long time.  It is piled up in a corner of the otherwise very nice sanctuary.  She updates you with stories of your mutual friends and about how the construction on the inside of the church is coming along.  Facha also seems happy to see you.  The dog runs in circles and wags its tail.  Alice laughs and tells you that Facha has been quite a naughty dog lately.  She has gotten into the habit of digging in the garden.  She thinks that the dog has even been burying odd things in the yard.  Alice gestures towards a table set with a Thanksgiving dinner that couldn't be beat.  There is stuffing, cranberry sauce, and an impressive turkey.  \par
\cf1 \par
sit\par
\cf2 You are now seated.\par
\cf1 \par
eat turkey\par
\cf2 As you enjoy the Thanksgiving Dinner That Couldn't Be Beat, Alice tells you that she has opened a restaurant.  "A restaurant?" you say.  "Not just any restaurant," she says.  "This is a special restaurant.  There will be no square meals there.  You should go see it later.  It's just a half a mile from the railroad track."  "Far out," you say, and finish your feast leaving only a large turkey bone on your plate.\par
\cf1 \par
take bone\par
\cf2 You pick up the bone.\par
\cf1 \par
give dog bone\par
\cf2 With a delighted bark, the dog grabs the bone and heads outside.  "You've made her day," says Alice.  "There she goes to dig in my yard again."  In a few moments, Facha returns, tracking in a fair ammount of dirt.\par
\cf1 \par
south\par
\cf2 You move south.\par
You are in front of a gothic wooden church.  The paint is peeling and the stained glass windows are in disrepair, but it retains much of its beauty and charm especially at this time of year.   Although the colors reached their peak a couple of weeks ago there are still enough orange leaves on the trees to remind you of a New England post card.  On the east side of the church you can make out Alice's garden.  Your VW microbus is parked here on a road heading north.  You'll have to get back in the bus if you want to go that way.  It's too far to walk.  There is a mailbox here.  You can move north and east.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
You are in Alice's garden.   Although the growing season has largely passed there are still some flowers and vegetables here.  The sunflowers seem to have toppled.  You are in Alice's garden.   The dog appears to have been busy.    There are several new holes in the ground and roots and bulbs have been brought to the surface along with some blue rocks.  These are slag from the old iron furnace that once supported the workers of the town.  They must have been buried for years.    Also here is an implement of destruction.  You can move north and west.\par
\cf1 \par
take implement of destruction\par
\cf2 You pick up an implement of destruction.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are at the stable.  Back in the days when this was an active church, it had room for 10 horses.  The stalls smell distinctly of manure and straw.   In the back of the stable there is an old cabinet of some kind.  Horse is here.  You can only move south.\par
\cf1 \par
play guitar\par
\cf2  Maybe it's just your imagination, but it seems like the horse is listening.  It has stopped eating for the moment and is swaying its head in time to the music.\par
