\cf2 You move south.\par
You are at a door with a sign on it that says "Room 604."\par
\cf1 \par
open door\par
\cf2 The door is now open.  The room is barren except for the psychiatrist's desk.  Psychiatrist is here.  "Come in my boy," says the psychiatrist.  He is apparently trying to put you at ease.  It is not working.  You enter room 604 anyway.  The psychiatrist looks at you intently and begins making notes on a pad of paper.  You think you hear him muttering something about "non-conformist," but maybe it's your imagination.  You sit down.  The shrink asks you some questions about your mother then asks you.  "Son, what do you want to do with your life?"\par
\cf1 \par
kill\par
\cf2 "Kill," you say.  "I want to kill.  I want to see blood and gore and guts and veins in my teeth.  Eat dead burnt bodies.  I mean kill."  And you start jumping up and down yelling "kill, kill..."  The psychiatrist starts jumping up and down with you yelling "kill, kill."  Now you're both jumping up and down yelling "kill, kill, kill, kill."  A sargeant is passing in the hall and when he hears the shouting he bursts into the room and pins a medal on your chest and says, "you're our boy."   He leads you from the room.  As you walk down the hall he asks you, "I just have one more question for you, kid.  Have you ever been arrested?"  You tell him the story of the Alice's Restaurant Masacree in 5 part harmony and he stops you and askes, "Kid, have you ever been to court?"  You tell him the story of the 27 8x10 color glossy photos with the circles and arrows... he stops you again and says, "Kid, I want you to go over there and sit down on that bench that says "Group W."  You walk in and join Group W.  This is where they put you if you may not be moral enough to join the army after committing your special crime.  There on the bench are mother rapers, father stabbers, father rapers, all sitting on the bench there next to you.\par
\cf1 \par
wait\par
\cf2 Time passes...\par
Father Raper walks towards you.  The meanest, nastiest, most horrible criminal of them all is summing you up.  He could snap you in half with his bare hands if he wanted to.  You're hoping he doesn't want to.  "So, what did you get?"  He asks you.  "I didn't get anything," you say, "I had to pay $25 and pick up the garbage."  "What was you arrested for?" he asks.\par
\cf1 \par
littering\par
\cf2 They all move away from you on the Group W bench.\par
\cf1 \par
and creating a nuissance\par
\cf2 They all move back and you have a great time talking about crime, mother stabbing father raping, until the Sargeant comes in.  He refers you to the paper you were given when you arrived at Whitehall Street.  He says, "Kidsthispieceofpapersgot47words37sentenceswewanttoknowthedetailsofthe crimeandeverythingpertainingtothecrimeandeverythingyougottosay..." and he talked like that for 45 minutes.  You fill out most of the paper with the details of your special crime, but then you turn the paper over and see the words "Kid, have you rehabilitiated yourself?"  \par
